  runtime). It concludes okay loses 3.1x. Both numbers are true; the
  question they answer is not the same one, and this page's own Lane
  Rule 2 forbids exactly this pairing. The benchmark ALREADY has the
  matched lanes on both sides — `forkJoin10k_kyoOutside` and
  `forkJoin10k_okayOwnInside` — so nothing needs writing, only
  reading.

  This is the SIXTH instance of the misnamed/mismatched pairing bug in
  this repository and the third I have made myself today, which is why
  the correction lands with the rule restated beside it.

